.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
# uv.lock is intentionally NOT ignored. It arrived in this file's initial
# commit alongside .venv/, __pycache__/ and .pytest_cache/ -- all derived
# artifacts -- but a lock is an input, and issue #160 Gate 7 requires a
# dependency lock sufficient for clean reproduction of every paper. An
# ignored lock makes that gate permanently unclosable.

# Ephemeral harness run state. The QG dual-harness runners create and rmtree
# these workspaces themselves, and the QG workflows upload artifacts/ as CI
# build artifacts rather than committing it. Lane receipts that carry authority
# are written to research/extensions/orion-qg/ and committed explicitly.
/artifacts/
/.orion-qg-*/
# LaTeX build intermediates. `latexmk` writes these beside `main.tex` on every
# build; only the `.pdf` is an artifact anyone reads. Leaving them untracked but
# unignored made a rebuild look like an uncommitted change to the manuscript.
#
# `.log`, `.out` and `.toc` are deliberately *not* ignored repository-wide: a
# campaign's `run.log` and `prepare.log` are evidence, and P11-P14 track a
# `paper/main.markdown.out`. Ignoring those extensions everywhere would silently
# drop a future evidence file from the index. So they are scoped to the one
# directory where they can only be TeX output.
papers/**/*.aux
papers/**/*.bbl
papers/**/*.blg
papers/**/*.fdb_latexmk
papers/**/*.fls
papers/**/*.synctex.gz
papers/**/manuscript/main.log
papers/**/manuscript/main.out
papers/**/manuscript/main.toc
papers/**/paper/main.log
papers/**/paper/main.out
papers/**/paper/main.toc
